    "done_when": "Two obligation hints computed in reckon/crew/obligations.py and rendered by reckon/hooks/coordinator_obligations.py stop misleading a coordinator. (1) review-missing is not listed while a review launched by the reflex holds a live claim for the reviewed run, and it is aged from the reflex's launch window, not from manifest completion. Measured on 2026-09-26: the hook listed review-missing with a ready-to-run dispatch command for worker-env-review-fixes and figure-as-text. The command was refused as a scope conflict because the reflex had already launched the review. (2) worktree-held names the live run that now occupies the worktree path, not a promoted run whose path was reused under the same node id. Measured the same day: the hook named promoted r-20260926T185645270593 while live r-20260926T193259670455 held the path, and gc correctly reported the tree live-referenced. tests/test_obligations_do_not_mislead.py uses tmp_path (the pytest fixture) with every crew directory environment-resolved to tmp_path. Case 1: a synthesised completed run with a live reflex review claim yields no review-missing item. Case 2: a promoted run and a live run sharing one worktree path yields a worktree-held item naming the live run id, or none. Negative control: the current logic; both cases must fail. tests/test_coordinator_obligations_hook.py, tests/test_crew_obligations.py and tests/test_mcp_crew_obligations.py add no failures against the base, with pytest basetemp outside any git repository. Gate and control logs are written under the run directory. The change is committed in this worktree.",
